  "steps": [
    "Brown the beef hard in the oil. A real sear, not a steam. That crust is the first layer of flavor.",
    "Add the onion, then the garlic.",
    "Toast the chili seasoning in the fat for about 30 seconds before adding any liquid. That wakes up the spices.",
    "Stir in the tomato paste, then the crushed tomatoes, beef broth, Worcestershire, soy sauce, brown sugar, and apple cider vinegar.",
    "Simmer on low for 1 1/2 to 2 hours. Leave it uncovered for the last 30 minutes so it tightens without flour.",
    "Beans are optional. If you use them, drain them and add them near the end.",
    "Stir the masa harina with 2 Tbsp water and mix that in at the end.",
    "Keep the cocoa in. It will not taste like chocolate.",
    "Day-two chili beats day-one chili. Refrigerate 4 to 5 days, or freeze up to 3 months."
  ],
